{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00285",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.61,
      "end_seconds": 3.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Okay, welcome. Let's see what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.34,
      "end_seconds": 5.04,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 6.28,
      "end_seconds": 10.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.16,
      "end_seconds": 14.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Please do. Extra information is always welcome. Was parking alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.08,
      "end_seconds": 21.1,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Not great, uh, I ended up a few streets away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.18,
      "end_seconds": 23.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Okay. Start wherever you like."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 25.19,
      "end_seconds": 27.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Well, he's been having constipation, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.75,
      "end_seconds": 32.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "And when did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.17,
      "end_seconds": 41.48,
      "duration_seconds": 8.31,
      "text": "Okay, so for four weeks, I'd say. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.77,
      "end_seconds": 46.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.95,
      "end_seconds": 62.13,
      "duration_seconds": 14.18,
      "text": "Only drinking more water, and it's not much. I'd give it a eight, out of ten. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite. I've also had a little bright blood on the paper, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.6,
      "end_seconds": 66.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Has there been a heavy feeling in the lower tummy too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.34,
      "end_seconds": 76.67,
      "duration_seconds": 9.33,
      "text": "Yeah. Nearly five years, I'd say. And there's straining to pass stool as well, two months now. About straining to pass stool, I'd say mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.02,
      "end_seconds": 81.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Have you had any black stools, weight loss or abdominal swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.72,
      "end_seconds": 85.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Well, no, none of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.03,
      "end_seconds": 87.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "So, what about vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.01,
      "end_seconds": 90.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "No, no vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 90.88,
      "end_seconds": 95.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice vomiting. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.17,
      "end_seconds": 101.39,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.97,
      "end_seconds": 108.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.53,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.78,
      "end_seconds": 111.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.92,
      "end_seconds": 115.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.23,
      "end_seconds": 119.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "So, uh, thank you, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.25,
      "end_seconds": 124.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.85,
      "end_seconds": 127.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Yes, shellfish. I get vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.1,
      "end_seconds": 130.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.07,
      "text": "How about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.59,
      "end_seconds": 134.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "No, I don't smoke and never have."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.04,
      "end_seconds": 137.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "What medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.45,
      "end_seconds": 146.87,
      "duration_seconds": 8.42,
      "text": "I take Thyronorm, 50 micrograms, every morning for my thyroid. I take glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 147.31,
      "end_seconds": 155.28,
      "duration_seconds": 7.97,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the glimepiride was 4 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.87,
      "end_seconds": 161.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Alright. Did you bring the up-to-date prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.34,
      "end_seconds": 165.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "I don't think I have it with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.69,
      "end_seconds": 173.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.58,
      "end_seconds": 184.05,
      "duration_seconds": 9.47,
      "text": "An underactive thyroid, for two years. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. Diabetes, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.81,
      "end_seconds": 185.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.05,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.57,
      "end_seconds": 189.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Let's get your blood pressure and the other basics."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.36,
      "end_seconds": 202.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Okay, give me a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.6,
      "end_seconds": 229.0,
      "duration_seconds": 7.4,
      "text": "Okay: pulse 86, respiratory rate 18. And saturation 97 percent, temperature 36.6, blood pressure 109 over 79."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.38,
      "end_seconds": 234.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.82,
      "end_seconds": 237.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Take a breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.23,
      "end_seconds": 259.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "I can feel firm stool in the left lower abdomen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.84,
      "end_seconds": 263.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Tell me if anything hurts as I press."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.65,
      "end_seconds": 274.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "There's no mass in the tummy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 275.49,
      "end_seconds": 276.19,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.5,
      "end_seconds": 300.53,
      "duration_seconds": 22.03,
      "text": "Right, that's fine, you can get dressed. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. Okay, so my impression is this: My working impression is chronic constipation. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. It could also be an underactive thyroid, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.69,
      "end_seconds": 308.16,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "I've, I've been thinking the worst, uh, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.27,
      "end_seconds": 328.29,
      "duration_seconds": 19.02,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like chronic constipation, but I'd like to confirm. I'm going to order a colonoscopy, for constipation and rectal bleeding. I'd like to arrange blood tests for constipation. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 328.85,
      "end_seconds": 331.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Sure, where do I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.54,
      "end_seconds": 354.17,
      "duration_seconds": 21.63,
      "text": "I'll start you on lactulose, 15 ml, at night, for two weeks. That's for constipation. More fibre, more water, and give yourself ten unhurried minutes after breakfast. Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.46,
      "end_seconds": 361.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.46,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 363.29,
      "end_seconds": 364.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 366.22,
      "end_seconds": 373.29,
      "duration_seconds": 7.07,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 374.53,
      "end_seconds": 376.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Oh, got it, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 378.22,
      "end_seconds": 384.98,
      "duration_seconds": 6.76,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in three weeks. Right, that's all I have. Is there anything you wanted to ask?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 386.31,
      "end_seconds": 388.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "No, you've explained it well. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}